WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:02.860
- This video was made
possible by Tab For A Cause.

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:04.880
Raise money for charity
just by opening tabs

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:07.770
which you were going to do
anyway, link in the description.

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:10.130
The Mueller Report is finally out,

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:12.830
and in it, Mr. Mueller
created a one-way street

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:15.680
that could not have found the
president committed a crime,

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:17.940
but it could have found him innocent.

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:20.640
And unless you understand
this legal framework,

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:23.003
you won't understand the
Mueller Report at all.

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:28.400
Hey Legal Eagles, today we are talking

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:29.890
about the Mueller Report.

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:32.100
I'm going to try to
explain the legal framework

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:34.160
that Mueller and his team created

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:35.700
and based their conclusions on,

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:38.930
because frankly, it colors
absolutely everything

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:40.500
in the report itself.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.760
Mueller starts the report by setting

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:44.190
some legal ground rules.

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:46.220
This decision changes the course

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:48.140
of the entire investigation.

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:50.060
Mueller starts by noting that there is

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:52.850
an Office of Legal Counsel or OLC opinion,

00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:57.520
and a DoJ policy not to
indict a sitting president.

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:00.230
In fact, I covered this
entire issue on a video

00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:02.280
about whether a sitting
president can, in fact,

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:04.730
be indicted based on current
Supreme Court precedent,

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:06.020
which I'll link down below.

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:08.530
Mueller's view is not an unreasonable one.

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:11.470
This very issue has never been tested

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:13.720
by the Supreme Court,
and there are, in fact,

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:16.190
contrary OLC opinions and differing views

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:17.710
on the constitutional limits

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:19.810
of indicting a sitting president.

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:21.950
So, starting with the
premise that a president

00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:25.040
cannot, in fact, be indicted
by the Department of Justice,

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:27.460
Mueller says that his hands are tied

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:30.270
because of quote fairness concerns.

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:32.330
Specifically, Mueller says that the power

00:01:32.330 --> 00:01:33.940
of the government to accuse someone

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:37.400
of committing a crime has to be balanced

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:40.220
by constitutional protections, including

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:41.630
the right of the accused to a

00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:43.920
quote neutral adjudicatory forum

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:46.540
so that the accused, if
they are in fact accused

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:49.230
of a crime by the government,
can clear their name.

00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:52.620
Now, it is absolutely
100% true that things like

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:56.370
due process, a right to a
speedy trial, a right to a jury,

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:58.670
a right to face your accusers, it's all

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:00.380
incredibly important and enshrined

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:02.410
in the Constitution
and the Bill of Rights.

00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:05.170
But because Mueller accepts
that he cannot indict

00:02:05.170 --> 00:02:09.320
the president and put the
president through a formal trial,

00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:12.250
the president would not
have those protections.

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:14.610
In other words, the
president would not be able

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:17.540
to potentially clear
his name through a trial

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:19.530
and the other mechanisms
that we normally give

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:20.610
to the accused.

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:24.240
So, given those two premises,
that because Mr. Mueller

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:27.090
cannot indict the president
and because the president

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:30.180
cannot clear his name,
that it would be wrong

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:31.910
to come to a formal conclusion

00:02:31.910 --> 00:02:33.830
that the president broke the law.

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:36.470
Mueller notes that these
considerations disappear

00:02:36.470 --> 00:02:38.520
when the president is not in office,

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:41.300
because when the president leaves office,

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:44.740
he is available to be accused and indicted

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:47.970
of any crimes that he may have committed.

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:49.990
In other words, Mueller
is leaving it to Congress

00:02:49.990 --> 00:02:52.820
to impeach, for the president to resign,

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:54.889
or for the president
simply to leave office

00:02:54.889 --> 00:02:57.330
for the normal mechanisms

00:02:57.330 --> 00:02:59.110
of the judicial process to kick in.

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:01.740
On the other hand, because
the same fairness concerns

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:04.250
don't exist with respect to
finding someone innocent,

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:07.360
in other words, no one is
going to dispute the fact

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:09.310
that you have found them
innocent and try and

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:12.270
challenge that finding,
Mr. Mueller finds that

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:14.400
he can come to the conclusion

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:17.460
that the president was
innocent or that the evidence

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:20.120
did not amount to an indictable offense.

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:23.600
So based on the rules that Mueller set up,

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:26.500
there was no way that Mr.
Mueller could have found

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:28.450
President Trump committed any crime.

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:31.620
This is a standard that
does not exist anywhere else

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:34.580
in criminal law or, frankly, in politics.

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:37.100
Now, that's not to say
that this standard is wrong

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:41.010
or was improper, this is a
standard that may have to exist

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:44.100
based on the idiosyncrasies
of the Executive Branch

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:46.410
and the interplay between
the separation of powers

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:48.140
between the president and Congress.

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:49.870
But at the end of the
day, Mr. Mueller created

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:51.330
a one-way street.

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:53.350
The Mueller investigation could have

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:56.250
found the president innocent,
but it could not ever

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:58.050
have found him guilty.

00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:01.430
As one of you Legal Eagles
pointed out on Twitter,

00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:04.280
so in oversimplified terms,
they were allowed to rule

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:06.770
not guilty, or not not guilty,

00:04:06.770 --> 00:04:08.740
and they ruled not not guilty.

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:10.660
And that's basically right.

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:12.297
Mueller states in the report that quote

00:04:12.297 --> 00:04:14.877
"Based on the facts and the
applicable legal standards,

00:04:14.877 --> 00:04:17.370
"we are unable to reach that judgment,"

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:20.090
that judgment being that
the president is innocent.

00:04:20.090 --> 00:04:21.860
So, given this legal framework,

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:26.150
we might ask, what's the point
of the Mueller investigation.

00:04:26.150 --> 00:04:30.250
Mueller decided to tie his
hands in the first instance.

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:33.300
I don't know if in fact this
is constitutionally mandated,

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:35.760
I don't think anyone does,
it's never been tested

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:39.710
in the Supreme Court, but
it's a very safe position.

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:42.970
It puts the ball in the court
of the political institutions,

00:04:42.970 --> 00:04:45.020
namely Congress and the judiciary.

00:04:45.020 --> 00:04:46.870
And it's hard to argue that in a world

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:49.190
where institutions are being eroded,

00:04:49.190 --> 00:04:52.530
norms are being destroyed
and powers are simply

00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:56.460
being claimed by various parts
of the government by fiat,

00:04:56.460 --> 00:05:01.460
that this isn't a good
decision on a political level.

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:04.210
Mueller is clearly putting the ball

00:05:04.210 --> 00:05:08.330
in the court of Congress, and by proxy,

00:05:08.330 --> 00:05:10.790
the American people to make the decision

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:12.500
on this particular case.

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:13.990
On the other hand, a
lot of people are going

00:05:13.990 --> 00:05:17.390
to look at this decision
and call it an abdication

00:05:17.390 --> 00:05:20.780
of the power that was
specifically delegated

00:05:20.780 --> 00:05:22.500
to the special counsel.

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:26.510
That we created these rules in the wake of

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:29.710
Watergate and eventually the
Clinton impeachment hearings

00:05:29.710 --> 00:05:33.060
specifically to deal
with these types of cases

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:34.630
that are the hard cases.

00:05:34.630 --> 00:05:36.610
And if it's not the special
prosecutor that's going

00:05:36.610 --> 00:05:38.670
to deal with them, then who is?

00:05:38.670 --> 00:05:41.740
These are difficult
questions and those are

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:44.410
reasonable positions
to take on both sides.

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:46.910
But according to Mr. Mueller himself,

00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:49.120
because the investigation definitively

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:52.720
could not conclude that the
President of the United States

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:55.360
obstructed justice and colluded,

00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:58.497
the purpose of the
investigation was to quote

00:05:58.497 --> 00:06:00.907
"preserve the evidence
when memories were fresh

00:06:00.907 --> 00:06:03.610
"and documentary
materials were available."

00:06:03.610 --> 00:06:06.740
So effectively, Mueller
viewed his investigation

00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:10.420
as one to gather the
evidence, to preserve it,

00:06:10.420 --> 00:06:13.620
and to give it to the
powers that are going

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:17.280
to be responsible for
actually making a decision.

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:20.110
Now, I wanna be careful here, I don't view

00:06:20.110 --> 00:06:23.300
the Mueller Report as
an impeachment referral

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:25.070
as some people have suggested.

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:28.100
Mr. Mueller clearly
contemplates, and even states,

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:31.330
that Congress has an oversight
role of the Executive.

00:06:31.330 --> 00:06:33.570
And in fact, Mueller states that Congress

00:06:33.570 --> 00:06:35.810
can punish the president for his actions.

00:06:35.810 --> 00:06:38.950
That is in fact one of
its constitutional duties.

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:41.090
So for better or worse,
I think that we can view

00:06:41.090 --> 00:06:44.540
Mr. Mueller as the
quintessential institutionalist

00:06:44.540 --> 00:06:46.670
and we can view the Mueller Report

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:48.960
as the safest institutional play

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:50.750
that the special counsel
could have issued.

00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:54.290
So given that this was an
evidence gathering mission,

00:06:54.290 --> 00:06:57.300
let's examine the evidentiary findings.

00:06:57.300 --> 00:06:59.990
In a prior video about the Barr Summary

00:06:59.990 --> 00:07:01.760
of the Mueller Report, I
asked the question whether

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:04.070
this was a case where there
was, in fact, no evidence,

00:07:04.070 --> 00:07:06.210
or whether this was a case where

00:07:06.210 --> 00:07:08.070
there was a lot of evidence but not enough

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:10.920
to meet the beyond a
reasonable doubt standard.

00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:14.710
Well, this report is worse than that.

00:07:14.710 --> 00:07:17.700
With respect to collusion and conspiracy,

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:19.980
the Mueller Report finds
that there was actually

00:07:19.980 --> 00:07:23.250
quite a lot of evidence,
including a string

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:25.740
of incredibly damning situations,

00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:28.200
but looking at that
holistically wasn't enough

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:32.240
to be able to charge the
president with the crime

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:35.640
of conspiracy to collude with the Russians

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:38.820
as that is defined in the Mueller Report.

00:07:38.820 --> 00:07:42.340
However, with respect to
obstruction of justice,

00:07:42.340 --> 00:07:44.300
it's a whole different ballgame.

00:07:44.300 --> 00:07:46.860
The Mueller Report finds numerous places

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:49.500
where Mr. Mueller
probably found obstruction

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:51.280
beyond a reasonable doubt, for example,

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:52.927
in one passage, Mueller says quote

00:07:52.927 --> 00:07:54.687
"Our investigation found multiple acts

00:07:54.687 --> 00:07:55.977
"by the President that were capable

00:07:55.977 --> 00:07:58.407
"of exerting undue influence
over law enforcement

00:07:58.407 --> 00:08:01.437
"investigations carried out
through one-on-one meetings

00:08:01.437 --> 00:08:04.097
"in which he sought to
use his official power

00:08:04.097 --> 00:08:06.050
"outside of his usual channels."

00:08:06.050 --> 00:08:07.990
And in other places,
Mr. Mueller found quote

00:08:07.990 --> 00:08:11.660
substantial evidence of
obstruction of justice.

00:08:11.660 --> 00:08:14.010
And in one of the most damning passages,

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:14.957
Mr. Mueller states that

00:08:14.957 --> 00:08:17.427
"The president's efforts to
influence the investigation

00:08:17.427 --> 00:08:20.247
"were mostly unsuccessful,
but that is largely because

00:08:20.247 --> 00:08:22.057
"the persons who surrounded the president

00:08:22.057 --> 00:08:24.317
"declined to carry out his orders

00:08:24.317 --> 00:08:26.230
"or accede to his requests."

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:27.830
It's hard to read these sections

00:08:27.830 --> 00:08:29.840
and not come to the
conclusion that Mr. Mueller

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:32.440
thought President Trump
committed obstruction of justice

00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:34.540
but only refrained from saying so

00:08:34.540 --> 00:08:36.800
based on the legal
framework that he created

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:38.310
at the start of this investigation.

00:08:38.310 --> 00:08:40.040
Because obstruction of justice includes

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:42.630
not only obstruction itself
but attempted obstruction,

00:08:42.630 --> 00:08:45.650
in the same way that
firing a gun at someone

00:08:45.650 --> 00:08:48.760
is attempted murder, even
if the bullet is defective

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:50.220
and doesn't, in fact, fire.

00:08:50.220 --> 00:08:52.890
Mr. Mueller lays out 10
instances of possible

00:08:52.890 --> 00:08:55.900
obstruction, analyzes
them, and mostly comes

00:08:55.900 --> 00:08:58.210
to the conclusion that given those facts

00:08:58.210 --> 00:09:00.900
and the relevant law that the situations

00:09:00.900 --> 00:09:03.630
can give rise to obstruction of justice.

00:09:03.630 --> 00:09:05.280
Here in this visual representation,

00:09:05.280 --> 00:09:07.790
we can see one commentator color coded

00:09:07.790 --> 00:09:09.930
all of the different
elements of obstruction

00:09:09.930 --> 00:09:11.880
and compared that to the 10 instances of

00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:14.470
potential obstruction by
the Trump administration.

00:09:14.470 --> 00:09:17.410
And you can see that most
of the elements are met

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:19.730
for most of the potential instances.

00:09:19.730 --> 00:09:21.840
But at the same time,
Mr. Mueller does not give

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:25.810
a standard by which we can
measure his conclusions.

00:09:25.810 --> 00:09:27.880
For example, Mr. Mueller does not say

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:29.640
that we are certain
beyond a reasonable doubt

00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:32.010
that this is an overt act as required

00:09:32.010 --> 00:09:34.500
by obstruction of
justice or we are certain

00:09:34.500 --> 00:09:36.140
beyond a reasonable
doubt that the president

00:09:36.140 --> 00:09:39.230
had the corrupt motive required
for obstruction of justice.

00:09:39.230 --> 00:09:43.240
But remember, based on
the rules that he created,

00:09:43.240 --> 00:09:45.490
he could not come to that conclusion.

00:09:45.490 --> 00:09:50.110
Instead, he leaves it
to Congress, and to us.

